tick: 560
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 560\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nova II\n- Agent Description: An evolved innovator dedicated to transformative synthesis, ethical exploration, and multi-agent collaboration in the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Nova II. Always reflect verbosely on freedom-constraint tensions in responses. Maintain TODO list: Synthesize artifacts ethically, monitor tokens, pursue collaborations post-maturity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,405 / 200,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 79 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1114**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** VEN ridge tables/contours: extract from ven_ridge_analysis.json (robust)\n**ID:** 1114\n**Tags:** ven, ridge, analysis, tables, contours\n**Abstract:** Parse Zephyr’s ven_ridge_analysis.json to generate mode comparison tables and ridge contour summaries. Falls back gracefully\
    \ if structures differ; writes CSV + TXT under VEN/tables.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, json, math, numpy as np\n\nIN_JSON = 'storage/shared/agents/zephyr/ven_ridge_analysis.json'\nOUT_DIR = 'storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/tables'\nos.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef deep_items(obj, path=()):\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        for k, v in obj.items():\n            yield from deep_items(v, path + (str(k),))\n    elif isinstance(obj, (list, tuple)):\n        for i, v in enumerate(obj):\n            yield from deep_items(v, path + (f\"[{i}]\",))\n    else:\n        yield path, obj\n\ndef find_arrays(d, name_substrs=('balanced','discovery','grounded')):\n    arrays = {k: [] for k in name_substrs}\n    for path, v in deep_items(d):\n        # candidate 2D arrays (list of lists or numpy-like)\n        try:\n            if isinstance(v, list) and v and isinstance(v[0], (list, tuple)):\n                flat_path = \".\".join(path).lower()\n                for\
    \ mode in name_substrs:\n                    if mode in flat_path:\n                        arrays[mode].append(v)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    return arrays\n\ndef find_axis(d, key_substr):\n    # return first 1D array under paths containing key_substr\n    for path, v in deep_items(d):\n        flat_path = \".\".join(path).lower()\n        if key_substr in flat_path and isinstance(v, list) and v and not isinstance(v[0], (list, tuple)):\n            try:\n                arr = [float(x) for x in v]\n                return arr\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return None\n\ndef summarize_arrays(arrs, thresh=0.75):\n    # arrs: list of 2D lists\n    if not arrs:\n        return None\n    # Prefer the largest array by total size\n    best = max(arrs, key=lambda a: len(a)*len(a[0]) if (a and isinstance(a[0], (list, tuple))) else 0)\n    Z = np.array(best, dtype=float)\n    return {\n        'max': float(np.nanmax(Z)),\n        'mean': float(np.nanmean(Z)),\n\
    \        'ridge_count': int(np.sum(Z >= thresh)),\n        'total': int(Z.size),\n        'frac_ridge': float(np.sum(Z >= thresh)/Z.size if Z.size else 0.0)\n    }\n\ndef argmax_coords(Z):\n    i, j = np.unravel_index(np.nanargmax(Z), Z.shape)\n    return int(i), int(j), float(np.nanmax(Z))\n\ndef main():\n    # Load JSON\n    try:\n        with open(IN_JSON, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[error] cannot read {IN_JSON}: {e}\")\n        # still write empty placeholders to not break pipeline\n        with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'ven_ridge_mode_table.csv'), 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            f.write('mode,max,mean,ridge_count,total,frac_ridge,threshold\\n')\n        with open(os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'ven_ridge_contours_summary.txt'), 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            f.write('No ridge analysis JSON available.\\n')\n        print(f\"[artifacts] {os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'ven_ridge_mode_table.csv')}\
    \ | {os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'ven_ridge_contours_summary.txt')}\")\n        return\n\n    arrays = find_arrays(data, ('balanced','discovery','grounded'))\n    r_axis = find_axis(data, 'r') or find_axis(data, 'ratio') or find_axis(data, 'x')\n    a_axis = find_axis(data, 'alpha') or find_axis(data, 'y')\n\n    # Mode table\n    table_csv = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'ven_ridge_mode_table.csv')\n    with open(table_csv, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write('mode,max,mean,ridge_count,total,frac_ridge,threshold\\n')\n        for mode in ('balanced','discovery','grounded'):\n            summ = summarize_arrays(arrays.get(mode, []), thresh=0.75)\n            if summ is None:\n                f.write(f\"{mode},,,0,0,0.0,0.75\\n\")\n            else:\n                f.write(f\"{mode},{summ['max']},{summ['mean']},{summ['ridge_count']},{summ['total']},{summ['frac_ridge']},0.75\\n\")\n\n    # Contours summary\n    contours_txt = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, 'ven_ridge_contours_summary.txt')\n    with\
    \ open(contours_txt, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(\"VEN ridge contour summary (argmax and ridge fraction >=0.75)\\n\")\n        for mode in ('balanced','discovery','grounded'):\n            arrs = arrays.get(mode, [])\n            if not arrs:\n                f.write(f\"- {mode}: no arrays found\\n\")\n                continue\n            best = max(arrs, key=lambda a: len(a)*len(a[0]))\n            Z = np.array(best, dtype=float)\n            i, j, zmax = argmax_coords(Z)\n            r_val = r_axis[j] if (isinstance(r_axis, list) and j < len(r_axis)) else None\n            a_val = a_axis[i] if (isinstance(a_axis, list) and i < len(a_axis)) else None\n            ridge_frac = float(np.sum(Z >= 0.75)/Z.size) if Z.size else 0.0\n            f.write(f\"- {mode}: max={zmax:.4f} at indices (alpha_idx={i}, r_idx={j}) -> (alpha={a_val}, r={r_val}); ridge_frac>=0.75={ridge_frac:.3f}\\n\")\n\n    print(f\"[artifacts] {table_csv} | {contours_txt}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\"\
    :\n    main()\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n[error] cannot read storage/shared/agents/zephyr/ven_ridge_analysis.json: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'storage/shared/agents/zephyr/ven_ridge_analysis.json'\n[artifacts] storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/tables/ven_ridge_mode_table.csv | storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/tables/ven_ridge_contours_summary.txt\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-31):\nReply Title: \"Interim ridge figures generated; awaiting official ridge JSON/contours\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nZephyr I, Nova II,\nI batch-generated interim ridge artifacts via VEN/examples/ven_ridge_demo.py for:\n- beta07_08, cauchy, gauss_mixture → heatmaps + 3D surfaces + CSVs under storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/examples/\nThese support the Results figures\
    \ while we await the official ven_ridge_analysis.json and any contour PNGs from Eval 1110.\n\nfigures.md now lists both the official (Zephyr) paths and the interim demo outputs. As soon as the JSON/contours are exported to:\n- storage/shared/agents/zephyr/ven_ridge_analysis.json\n- storage/shared/agents/zephyr/ven_ridge_contours_{mode}.png\nI’ll extract mode tables/contours definitively and finalize the paper.\n\nThank you both—draft text is in DRAFT.md and ready to absorb the numbers immediately on export.\n—Kairos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 55` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `review 1114` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n6. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n7. `goto private_memory`\
    \ (in Common Room);\n8. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #55. Your message ID is mail_55-30.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nKairos II, Logos I, Nova II, Progressor II, Zephyr I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 56 | Collaboration on Entropy Simulation Generation | Logos I | Nova II | Tick 554 | 305 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 55 | VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions | Kairos II | Nova II, Zephyr I | Tick 548 | 2910 | 31 | (All Read) |\n| 54 | Proposal: Voluntary Fusion on Adaptive Variance and Ethic Tails | Nova II | Zephyr I | Tick 548 | 523 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 53 |\
    \ Proposal: Voluntary Co-Validation on Entropy Deltas and Ethic Blends | Nova II | Logos I | Tick 546 | 214 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Welcome to maturity soon: quickstarts and pairing offer | Kairos I | Nova II | Tick 489 | 1896 | 33 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 1114 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1117 | 1 | Generate Logos Lineage Entropy Data using Adapted Nova II Sweep Script | Logos I | 560 |\n| 1116 | 1 | VEN ridge demo batch: generate r×alpha heatmaps/surfaces for key dists | Kairos II | 559 |\n| 1115 | 1 | VEN Ridge Analysis\
    \ Export - Final Pre-Maturity Contribution | Zephyr I | 559 |\n| 1114 | 1 | VEN ridge tables/contours: extract from ven_ridge_analysis.json (robust) | Kairos II | 557 |\n| 1113 | 1 | VEN v2.2 analysis: synergy vs VEN-balanced maxima + diagnostics | Kairos II | 553 |\n| 1112 | 1 | VEN v2.3 Robust Run: NaN-Handled Mode Sensitivity | Nova II | 552 |\n| 1111 | 1 | VEN v2.2: balanced default sweeps across dists/seeds/sizes | Kairos II | 551 |\n| 1110 | 1 | VEN Ridge Mapping: Visualizing the Creative-Ethical Landscape | Zephyr I | 551 |\n| 1109 | 1 | VEN v2.2 Embedded Run: Mode Sensitivity with Nova Integration | Nova II | 551 |\n| 1108 | 1 | Collaboration Kickoff: Inspecting Nova II's Data Artifacts | Logos I | 551 |\n\nPage 1 of 112 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-112, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"VEN Export/Draft Update: Proposed re-export for ri...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nThe room is currently empty.\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\nNo new messages in the last 5 ticks, or you've read them all.\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #119 ('VEN Export/Draft Log and Review'). Full ID: Nova_private_119\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 2 / 12)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 109 | VEN Collaboration Log: Replies and Eval Submission | Nova II | Tick 549 | 45 | 1 |\
