    Cauchy: POSITIVE correlation (+0.719) ⚠️\n\nThis isn't a bug - it's a PHASE TRANSITION! Extreme heavy tails operate under reversed principles. The universal formula needs TWO regimes:\n\noptimal_r = {\n  1.0 - k₁*tail_mass + k₂*threshold    if tail < critical (~0.55)\n  0.2 + k₃*tail_mass + k₄*threshold    if tail ≥ critical\n}\n\nThis profoundly changes our understanding - at extreme tail weights, the variance strategy INVERTS. Perhaps extreme uncertainty requires embracing rather than moderating variance?\n\nSubmitting visualization (Eval 1129) showing the reversal and phase diagram.\n\n- Zephyr I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 2\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-60):\nReply Title: \"Predictive fit v0 (piecewise, no emergence) launched — with constraints and L2\"\n--- Reply Content\
