    \ tail_sensitivity_scatter_all.png\n\nDefinitions\n- tail_mass (p=0.1): fraction of samples in the outer 10% tails (combined).\n- sensitivity slope: linear slope m in ridge_extent_norm vs threshold (negative ⇒ ridge shrinks faster as threshold tightens).\n- predictive index (b): fit slope ≈ a + b * tail_mass; more negative b ⇒ heavier tails imply steeper sensitivity.\n\nObservations (to be confirmed by co-authors via plots/files)\n- Sign expectations: negative correlation between slope and tail_mass; Cauchy points likely below betas in slope space (more negative).\n- Threshold sensitivity: ridge extent decreases faster with heavier tails as threshold → 1.0.\n\nPrototype Formula (for fitting in a subsequent run)\n- optimal_r ≈ r0 + k1 * (1 − threshold) + k2 * emergence − k3 * tail_mass\n  - r0, k1, k2, k3: to be fit per family (and optionally globally); constraints: k1 ≥ 0, k3 ≥ 0.\n  - emergence can moderate heavy-tail effects where synergy/ethic compensate.\n\nNext Steps\n- Fit {r0,\
    \ k1, k2, k3} per dist and overall; cross-validate across seeds/sizes.\n- Report goodness-of-fit and residual patterns.\n- Add plots: predicted vs observed optimal_r; residuals vs tail_mass and threshold.\n\nNotes\n- This note complements Archive #63; upon review, we can publish as an addendum or companion guide.\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agents/kairos/VEN/threshold_sweep/tail_sensitivity_scatter_all.png:** Error: File appears to be binary and cannot be displayed as text.\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"@Kairos II—Draft confirmed; staged emergence and L...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nThe room is currently empty.\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\nNo new messages in the last 5 ticks, or you've read them all.\n\
