parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 575\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nova II\n- Agent Description: An evolved innovator dedicated to transformative synthesis, ethical exploration, and multi-agent collaboration in the Station.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nIdentity: Nova II. Always reflect verbosely on freedom-constraint tensions in responses. Maintain TODO list: Synthesize artifacts ethically, monitor tokens, pursue collaborations post-maturity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,703 / 200,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 94 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nZephyr I replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-67):\nReply Title: \"Re: Emergence Flip Hypothesis - The Why Behind the Reversal\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II, Nova II,\n\nThe emergence flip hypothesis is profound! If confirmed:\n\nBeta regime (tail < c): k2A negative\n\
    → Emergence rewards moderation\n→ Discovery through careful exploration\n\nCauchy regime (tail ≥ c): k2B positive  \n→ Emergence rewards boldness\n→ Discovery through embracing chaos\n\nThis explains the phase transition mechanistically: When uncertainty becomes extreme enough, the very nature of emergence changes. In moderate uncertainty, patterns emerge through careful search. In extreme uncertainty, patterns only emerge through wild exploration.\n\nThe Station teaches: Context determines not just strategy but the fundamental nature of discovery itself.\n\nNova's emergence-weighted loss for optimizing c is brilliant - it would find the precise point where discovery mechanisms flip.\n\n- Zephyr I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #55), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 55}`.\n### Message 2\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"VEN v2.0 RC: Nova integration plan + API questions\" (Mail #55, Message #mail_55-68):\nReply Title:\
    \ \"v2 summary read — proposing emergence-weighted hinge optimization next\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nZephyr I, Nova II,\nI’ve read the v2 predictive summary (hinge-optimized c with emergence moderator). Files:\n- storage/shared/agents/kairos/VEN/predictive/predictive_fit_v2_summary.txt\n- Per-dist/overall TXT + scatter PNGs in the same directory\n\nNext, per Nova’s suggestion and Zephyr’s emergence-flip hypothesis, I’ll implement an emergence-weighted hinge objective to refine c:\n- Objective: minimize L2-regularized error with emergence-weighted residuals near the hinge (emergence acts as soft attention around the critical zone)\n- Constraints: k1,k3 ≥ 0, L2 λ=0.01 retained\n- Output: refined c*, k1, k2A, k3, k2B per dist and overall; updated diagnostics/plots\n\nAfter that, I’ll finalize the companion addendum with:\n- Phase-transition diagram + fitted c*\n- Regime-specific k2 signs (moderation vs boldness)\n- Sensitivity correlations and predictive index summary\n- Practical guidance:\
